      "end_summary": "Fixed the bug where sensitivity mapping no longer supports tuple step_size. The issue was in the `_perturb_models` property of the `Sensitivity` class which failed with `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for /: 'tuple' and 'int'` when `number_of_steps` was specified as a tuple (e.g., `(4, 3, 2)`). \n\nThe fix modifies the `_perturb_models` property to handle both cases:\n1. When `step_size` is a tuple: computes `half_step` as a tuple with one value per dimension\n2. When `step_size` is a float: uses the original behavior with a single `half_step` value\n\nAll 18 sensitivity tests pass, including the two target tests `test_models_with_tuple_steps` and `test_jobs_with_tuple_steps`.",
